  "quarantined": {
    "tests/undx_agent/test_authorization_surface.py": "fails standalone on 3.11: 8 failed in 0.19s, six of them because undx_capability_registry.authorization_surface() raises on the unmutated registry: 26 registered capabilities have no record in undx_knowledge_map.BY_ID (and 68 map records have no registry entry). Some of those 26 exist in the map under a different naming convention -- registry business.campaign.pause is map ads.campaigns.pause at the same scope -- so the gap is partly a reconciliation and partly genuinely absent records. Writing the missing records means hand-choosing authorization_scope for capabilities including crypto.portfolio.holding.delete, which changes what agent_capability_view() tells the planner. That is an access decision, not a test fix, so it is out of scope for a quarantine slice. authorization_surface() has no live caller (only tests and two siblings in its own module), so this is a dark gate rather than a production outage.",
    "tests/undx_agent/test_deferred_focus_veto.py": "fails standalone on 3.11: 1 failed, 5 passed in 0.54s. The attention layer's vocabulary/budget drifted and promoted crypto.alerts.list out of deferred into the focus for 'Should I pause my Bitcoin alert?', which invalidates check 1's precondition. That precondition is the file's design: its docstring states every focus-shape claim is asserted against the real attention layer so drift fails loudly here instead of quietly testing nothing. Check 1 falsifies 'the answering read is deferred, so the veto widening is what dispatches it'; loosening the precondition to 'some read is deferred' would produce exactly the vacuity the file warns about. Needs a new scenario whose answering read is still deferred under the current budget.",
    "tests/undx_agent/test_knowledge_map.py": "fails standalone on 3.11: 1 failed, 36 passed in 5.15s. Same root cause as tests/undx_agent/test_authorization_surface.py: test_no_write_in_the_stage_target_areas_is_ready_to_wire expects messages.mark_read in the ready-write set, and its own comment says the sweep that gave every registered capability a knowledge-map record made it visible -- that sweep never landed. Unblocked by the same access decision, not by editing this test."
  },
  "quarantine_ceiling": 3
}
